// Track G.3 (coloring) — a `yield` belongs to the innermost enclosing generator, and a closure is a
// fresh function boundary (its own return, not the generator's `Iterator<T>`). So a `yield` inside a
// closure — here one passed to the `map` builtin — is not inside a generator and is rejected (E0039),
// rather than silently suspending the wrong frame. The generator's own top-level `yield` is fine; it
// is the one inside the callback that is colored out.
// expect: error E0039 at 9:33
// expect: exit 1
fn g(): Iterator<int> {
    ys = map([1, 2, 3], fn(n) { yield n; return n; });
    yield 0
}
echo g().collect()
